{"kind":"event","event_id":2929,"event_uid":"01M2J65SWP1CDNV4DWMWEVA844","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":155,"issue_uid":"01M2J63P4Q920E5FVNNRK3EWC2","issue_short_id":"ewc2","actor":"impl:1@run-138","hlc_physical_ms":1789464340374,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"355f6a723a3ed30c6555cd0896c6c1bd9466df6a7be41f85f7641efc5b041413","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J65SWN93EK0BT3NR9W13S9","author":"impl:1@run-138","body":"Task 1: rewriting skills/ultrapowers/references/report-format.md so its sentences describe the ready-set engine at 597c6db1 rather than the retired wave loop. Plan: waveMerges row -> one row per epoch (wave = the epoch); waves row -> the plan's compiled layering, a waveMerges wave is an epoch not an index into it; unfinished row -> the three engine strings (never dispatched / depends on a failed task / predecessor never landed) with 'never became ready' and 'reason'; blockedWaves + missingDeliverables -> never-ready instead of cascade-blocked; status section cut to three bullets MERGED/CONFLICT/TEST_FAILED; judgmentCalls binding kinds -> endpoint not in run, dependency cycle; Presentation 2/5/6/9 read per epoch. Leaving tasks[].review (pinned by tests/test_review_peer.py) byte-for-byte.","created_at":"2026-09-15T09:25:40.373260197Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T09:25:40.374Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2931,"event_uid":"01M2J6605BWSDN5T59ESQ8GJ56","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":156,"issue_uid":"01M2J63SJPS72VC3ZEDWY1P30M","issue_short_id":"p30m","actor":"impl:2@run-138","hlc_physical_ms":1789464346795,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"05014e32859ce2a10047328cd5760f5965efadb08572bf898abdea0e9396abfc","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J6605AWSSEJY78XFXZA7Y7","author":"impl:2@run-138","body":"Approach for task 2 (re-edged reads waiting): one new branch in the sandbox-boot projection — `elif kind == \"driver:re-edged\"` sets state[tid]=\"waiting\" and blocked_by[tid]=[str(s) for s in listed(doc,\"blockedBy\")], with blocked_by a new dict beside proof/park/attention and \"blockedBy\": blocked_by.get(tid) added as the LAST key of every task cell. Events are id-sorted, so a re-edge after a BLOCKED end wins, a BLOCKED end with no re-edge stays failed, and a later worker:start moves the state on through the existing start rule while blocked_by is never cleared. Then CONTRACT.md's **status.json:** bullet (waiting into the state enum, a \"blockedBy\" cell in the literal, eight→nine states, one sentence on the event) and RUNBOOK.md's Watch. entry for status.json. I do not write fleet/tests/test_sandbox_boot_viz.mjs — that path is the peer's exam.","created_at":"2026-09-15T09:25:46.794662115Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T09:25:46.795Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2933,"event_uid":"01M2J67R2WSZSESTPZAWS62CG3","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":156,"issue_uid":"01M2J63SJPS72VC3ZEDWY1P30M","issue_short_id":"p30m","actor":"exam:2@run-138","hlc_physical_ms":1789464404060,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"2f95c23aeef2408c0e53578434002b7f271a5d44046afa81b40f06a584071b1c","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J67R2T69NJT1GQTCGKQRAD","author":"exam:2@run-138","body":"examiner (task 2, exam `fleet/tests/test_sandbox_boot_viz.mjs`): approach I am taking.\n\nThe exam is run-97's standing file extended a third time. Plan:\n\n1. `cell()` (line 112) gains `blockedBy: null` as its LAST key — that is what makes leg (b)'s whole-object pins (`TASKS_WITH_ARGS`, `TASKS_NO_ARGS`) and case (c)'s live-page pins read the new seven-key shape, and it is the reason the file is red at BASE.\n2. The three inline cell literals that spell the six keys out by hand rather than through `cell()` — leg (b)'s three `deepEqual`s on `doc.tasks['1'|'2'|'3']` and leg (d)'s pin on `second.tasks['6']` — each gain `blockedBy: null` in the same last position. They are the same assertions they were at BASE; M3 says every cell the verb prints carries the key, so a literal without it would go red for the wrong reason.\n3. New block `(#987 a)`–`(#987 f)` after the #952 block, on `[...B, BLOCKED_END_15, ev(16, {kind:'driver:re-edged', task:'2', blockedBy:['1']})]`:\n   - (a) M1 — that log projects `tasks['2']` deep-equal `cell({state:'waiting', blockedBy:['1']})`; `role` null because `BLOCKED_END_15` closed `impl:2`.\n   - (b) M2 — the same log WITHOUT the re-edge line projects `cell({state:'failed'})`, whose `blockedBy` is `null`. Whole-cell, so a projection that reads every BLOCKED end as waiting fails here.\n   - (c) M3 — the fourteen-line `B` with `ARGS_JSON` deep-equals `TASKS_WITH_ARGS`, and each of the three cells' `Object.keys` is exactly `['wave','state','role','lastProof','park','attention','blockedBy']` — the Produces line's own order, which pins both 'blockedBy is last' and 'the other six read as at BASE'.\n   - (d) M4 — leg (a)'s log plus `start(17,'impl:2','implementer')` projects `cell({state:'implementing', role:'impl:2', blockedBy:['1']})`: the start rule moves the state and `blocked_by` is never cleared.\n   - (e) M5 — the first two `Run:` lines, verbatim, as `shOk`/exact-count over the `**status.json:**` bullet scoped to the `**Publish:**` bullet: `queued|waiting|examining`, a `\"blockedBy\":` cell, `nine states above`, and zero lines saying `eight states`.\n   - (f) M6 — the third `Run:`, the runbook's **Watch.** `status.json` entry scoped to the `events.jsonl` entry, matching `queued.*waiting.*failed`.\n\nReading of a leg worth recording: standing leg (f)'s eight-state loop (line 750) is left as it stands — all eight names survive the edit, so the loop is still true — and `waiting` is pinned in the new (#987 e) instead. That keeps the loop's 'all eight' sentence honest rather than making it stale.\n\nNo document sentence is cited as evidence of code behaviour: (a)–(d) are the sim, (e)–(f) are scoped greps.","created_at":"2026-09-15T09:26:44.058908668Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T09:26:44.06Z"}
